# Polarity SC Dark for WebCLAP

This is an experimental browser port. It is not an official Polarity release.

- Original plugin: https://github.com/polarity/plugin.nih.polarity-sc-dark
- Original revision: cc990a190545c515b590b05d5e0f4cdcae175b5b (version 0.5.4).
- This port and its build recipe: @SOURCE_URL@
- Build command: `scripts/build-sc-dark.sh`.

## License

The SC Dark plugin and this port use GPL-3.0-or-later. See `LICENSE`.
The original authors are Robbert van der Helm and Robert Polarity Agthe.

The Rust framework is NIH-plug, licensed under ISC. See `licenses/NIH-plug-ISC.txt`.
This port does not link JUCE or replace the repository's MIT license.
The browser interface uses system fonts. It does not bundle external fonts or images.

The accompanying source archive contains the pinned upstream source, its Cargo.lock,
the patch, browser interface, build scripts, help, and tests.
Cargo.lock identifies the Rust dependency versions and Git revisions.
Cargo obtains those dependencies from their recorded sources during a build.
`licenses/dependencies.json` records the plugin dependency graph, including build and test dependencies.
The matching license texts are in `licenses/dependencies/`.
RealFFT 3.5.0 declares MIT but contains no license text in its package or recorded upstream revision.
Its original Cargo.toml and README are included as evidence. Review this omission before public binary distribution.
Rust library notices and license texts are in `licenses/Rust-library.html` and `licenses/rust/`.

The original compression and FFT algorithms remain unchanged.
The port replaces the desktop interface and adds WebCLAP glue, presets, and help.

This software has no warranty. See the license for details.
